ate edge justify a slightly narrower margin than the ratings imply, but not a change in the likely outcome.", "watch": "Any late polling showing Munson within single digits, or a major fundraising or outside-spending surge behind her, would signal the race is tightening beyond current expectations.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Kevin Stitt (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Oklahoma's governorship is open this year as term limits keep Kevin Stitt off the ballot, leaving Republicans to nominate state Senator Mike Mazzei against House Minority Leader Cyndi Munson, the Democrat. The state's strong Republican tilt frames the contest, and every major race rater calls it Safe or Solid Republican, with one rating it Likely Republican. Prediction markets similarly give Democrats only a small chance of an upset.\n\nThe campaign has been competitive in tone: the two met in a sole televised debate in early October, trading jabs on tribal relations and abortion, and the Democratic Governors Association claimed a debate win for Munson. President Trump also campaigned in Oklahoma for Mazzei. Still, with no public polling available and the state's partisan lean so pronounced, Munson would need a substantial shift in fundamentals to overcome the Republican advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -13.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0251, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0363, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0321, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.018, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0192, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0194, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02"